.\" -*- mode: troff; coding: utf-8 -*-
.TH AMU\-RESOLV 8
.SH NAME
amu\-resolv \- Qwaderton Linux dependency graph resolver
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
\fBamu\-resolv\fR is the single owner of the dependency graph. It
resolves package dependencies against the recipe repositories in
\fBAMU_REPO\fR (synchronized with \fBreposync\fR(8)), which are the
same repositories \fBamu\-src\fR(8) builds from and \fBamu\-bin\fR(8)
uses as its source of truth, so dependency resolution is identical for
source builds and binary installs.
.LP
Dependencies come from the \fIdepends\fR and \fImakedepends\fR files
next to each recipe, with \fBAMU_ALIAS\fR substitution applied.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR \fI<pkg>\fR
Print the direct dependencies of \fI<pkg>\fR, one per line.
.TP
\fB\-dd\fR \fI<pkg>\fR
Like \fB\-d\fR, but includes \fImakedepends\fR.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR \fI<pkg...>\fR
Print the full dependency closure of the named packages in install
order (dependencies before dependents), one per line.
.TP
\fB\-DD\fR \fI<pkg...>\fR
Like \fB\-D\fR, but includes \fImakedepends\fR.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR \fI<pkg>\fR
Print the packages that directly depend on \fI<pkg>\fR (reverse
dependencies, "dependents").
.TP
\fB\-jj\fR \fI<pkg>\fR
Like \fB\-j\fR, but also considers \fImakedepends\fR.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Print help and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBAMU_REPO\fR
Space-separated recipe repository directories. Required.
.TP
\fBAMU_RESOLV_SKIP_INSTALLED\fR
Skip already-installed packages during \fB\-D\fR/\fB\-DD\fR traversal.
Used internally by \fBamu\-bin\fR(8).
.TP
\fBAMU_ALIAS\fR
Dependency substitution, \fIreal:alias\fR space-separated pairs.
.TP
\fBAMU_ROOT\fR
Alternative install root used to locate the installed package database
(default \fI/\fR).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amu (8),
.BR amu\-bin (8),
.BR amu\-src (8)

